Description: Fail closed when dropping privileges
 drop_privileges() only logged a warning and continued when the
 configured nrpe_user/nrpe_group could not be resolved or when
 setgid()/setuid()/SETEUID() failed, leaving the daemon (or plugin
 children) running with more privileges than configured. Each failure
 now returns ERROR; the daemon aborts startup and plugin children exit
 before popen() instead of executing commands as root.
 initgroups() EPERM remains non-fatal: it is the expected result when
 the daemon is started as an unprivileged user (e.g. systemd User=).
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-02 22:54:59.604278211 +0200
+++ b/src/nrpe.c	2026-10-03 00:08:47.103927092 +0200
@@ -574,7 +574,10 @@
